{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"MAJOR SCOPE CORRECTION discovered via research: findings.py's shared SEVERITIES/normalize_finding/Finding.severity field is used by an entire completion-verification module cluster (completion_reconcile.py, completion_child_gate.py, epic_bug_screen.py, workflow/gate_ops.py, workflow/completion_verdict_assembly.py -- all hardcode severity=\"high\" as their ONLY signal, zero priority/decision/impact concept) that is genuinely UNRELATED to the epic's motivating bug (pass3_decide's impact-only severity_label vs priority). Ticket 6's original plan to delete severity from findings.py's shared vocabulary would break this entire cluster with no fallback. Corrected architecture: only the review-kernel (pass3_decide) stops STAMPING severity onto its own findings; findings.py's shared SEVERITIES/normalize_finding/Pydantic field stay untouched (serve non-kernel producers); common.schema.json's severity requirement is RELAXED to optional (not deleted) -- non-breaking per docs/api-stability.md since existing producers keep providing it. This significantly narrows and de-risks ticket 6, and likely means the ADR needs a follow-up amendment. Checking now whether ticket 5 (fail_on_severity workflow gate) has the same latent issue -- does the `gate` workflow step in steps.py only ever see kernel-produced (priority-bearing) findings, or could it also run on completion-verification/spec_scan findings that would default to priority 0.0 and silently stop failing the gate?"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788132181692474762,"uuid":"ca06a02b-fdce-4128-bb6d-903acbd7b1eb"}